speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, I wonder if the Secretary of State would check with the various departments of government which hire workers, especially in the northland, and recommend to them that they pay one scale of wages for a particular job. What is happening now, usually in regard to the hiring of native labour, is that the Department of Northern Affairs and National Resources will hire an Indian to do labouring work and pay him $1.20 an hour. The Department of Citizenship and Immigration will hire a native in the same community to do labouring work and pay him $1.00 an hour;
1380	HOUSE OF
Supply-Mines and Technical Surveys then some other department will come in and hire the same people as labourers at $1.40. I wonder if the Secretary of State will take the trouble to advise the departments concerned that the rates should be the same, and I hope she will recommend the highest rate.
